WEBVTT

00:00:01.690 --> 00:00:11.070
<v Ira Glass>Ladies and gentlemen, public radio listeners everywhere, now let us praise famous crap, OK, and not so famous crap too.
<v Ira Glass>女士们先生们，世界各地的公共广播听众们，现在让我们来赞美一下那些著名的垃圾，好吗？当然，还有那些不太出名的垃圾。

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:15.490
<v Starlee Kine>Well, there's a show called Boy Meets World . You ever seen it?
<v Starlee Kine>嗯，有个节目叫《男孩遇见世界》。你看过吗？

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:16.260
<v Ira Glass>No.
<v Ira Glass>没有。

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:17.560
<v Starlee Kine>It's great. It's so good.
<v Starlee Kine>它很棒。真的非常好。

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:18.440
<v Ira Glass>It's in syndication?
<v Ira Glass>它在重播吗？

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:22.660
<v Starlee Kine>Yeah, it's one of those shows that just went under the radar.
<v Starlee Kine>是的，它就是那种被忽视的节目之一。

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:54.750
<v Ira Glass>Friends, we are not here today to talk about those supposedly good TV programs people who think that they're smart like to talk about when they talk about TV. We're here to talk about the stuff that makes up so much of TV. We're here to speak of reruns. And not good reruns at that, I'm talking your Matlock s, your Living Singles , your Kate & Allies . This voice you are hearing is Starlee Kine, one of the producers of our radio program. And I asked her to talk about her relationship to TV, because she's the first person I've ever met who actively prefers reruns like Boy Meets World .
<v Ira Glass>朋友们，我们今天不是来谈论那些自以为聪明的人在谈论电视时喜欢谈论的所谓好节目的。我们是来谈论那些构成电视大部分内容的节目的。我们是来谈论重播的。而且还不是那种好的重播，我说的是《马特洛克》、《独身生活》、《凯特与艾莉》这类。你听到的这个声音是斯塔莉·凯恩，我们广播节目的制作人之一。我请她谈谈她与电视的关系，因为她是我认识的第一个主动偏爱《男孩遇见世界》这类重播节目的人。

00:00:54.750 --> 00:01:03.720
<v Starlee Kine>And it just like was on for years, but you never knew it. And now it's just like permanently in reruns, and it's on like four different channels. But it's not very good.
<v Starlee Kine>它播了好几年，但你根本不知道。现在它就像永久处于重播状态，在四个不同的频道播出。但它其实并不怎么好看。

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:05.640
<v Ira Glass>In fact, is it actually bad?
<v Ira Glass>事实上，它真的很烂吗？

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:09.740
<v Starlee Kine>I think so. I mean, it's hard for me to tell at this point, but it's bad, yeah.
<v Starlee Kine>我想是吧。我是说，现在我很难分辨，但它确实很烂。

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:11.850
<v Ira Glass>So if it's bad, why are you watching?
<v Ira Glass>既然很烂，你为什么还要看？

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:16.020
<v Starlee Kine>It's very, very, very comforting to watch it.
<v Starlee Kine>看它非常、非常、非常令人舒心。

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:19.120
<v Ira Glass>It's comforting because you used to watch it when you were a little kid?
<v Ira Glass>令人舒心是因为你小时候经常看它？

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:19.720
<v Starlee Kine>No.
<v Starlee Kine>不。

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:20.540
<v Ira Glass>You never saw it as a kid?
<v Ira Glass>你小时候从没看过？

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:52.820
<v Starlee Kine>No, not that one. But Boy Meets World , it's like it didn't even matter that I didn't watch it as a little kid. I can imagine little kids being in really comfortable, carpeted family rooms and laying with their elbows propped up and watching Boy Meets World and feeling really safe. Because it's like the safest thing in the world. This family is so nuclear, it's perfect. But it's soundstages, and it looks really fake. The principal is also the kid's neighbor. You know what I mean? He's just always there and always looking after everyone.
<v Starlee Kine>没有，没看过那部。但《男孩遇见世界》，我小时候没看过也无所谓。我可以想象小孩子们在非常舒适、铺着地毯的家庭房里，胳膊肘支着躺在那儿，看着《男孩遇见世界》，感觉非常安全。因为它就像世界上最安全的东西。这个家庭非常核心，非常完美。但那是摄影棚布景，看起来真的很假。校长还是那个孩子的邻居。你明白我的意思吗？他总是出现在那里，总是照顾每个人。

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:53.550
<v William Russ In Boy Meets World>Hey son, how was your day?
<v William Russ In Boy Meets World>嘿，儿子，你今天过得怎么样？

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:54.240
<v Ben Savage In Boy Meets World>Fine.
<v Ben Savage In Boy Meets World>挺好。

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:54.780
<v William Russ In Boy Meets World>What did you do in school?
<v William Russ In Boy Meets World>你在学校做什么了？

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:55.230
<v Ben Savage In Boy Meets World>Nothing.
<v Ben Savage In Boy Meets World>什么都没做。

00:01:55.230 --> 00:02:08.580
<v William Russ In Boy Meets World>Hey, hold on right there. You know, every day I ask you, what did you do. And every day you tell me, nothing. Well, I'm tired of nothing. I mean, we both know something happened today. And I want to know what it is.
<v William Russ In Boy Meets World>嘿，等一下。你知道，我每天都问你做了什么。而你每天都告诉我，什么都没做。好吧，我厌倦了“什么都没做”。我是说，我们都知道今天发生了什么事。我想知道那是什么。

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:11.920
<v Ben Savage In Boy Meets World>I decided to be a girl.
<v Ben Savage In Boy Meets World>我决定当个女孩。

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:29.360
<v Starlee Kine>I would imagine, if I were a little kid watching it, I'd feel so secure. Knowing that there's kids out there who feel secure is enough for me to feel comforted by it and watch it every time its on.
<v Starlee Kine>我想，如果我是个看这部剧的小孩，我会感到很安心。知道外面有孩子感到安心，这就足以让我感到慰藉，并且每次它播出时我都会看。

00:02:29.360 --> 00:03:00.360
<v Starlee Kine>I try very hard to establish these things so that I have these reruns, because I live in eternal fear that the reruns are going to be gone. Like last night, I was watching TV and I couldn't find a rerun anywhere and I was panicking. The Godfather was on, and I was flipping, flipping, and I couldn't find one. I was just like, how is this possible? There was a rerun though. It was a rerun of The Nanny was on. And I don't have any relationship with it, so I was stuck.
<v Starlee Kine>我非常努力地确立这些东西，这样我才有这些重播节目可以看，因为我一直生活在一种永恒的恐惧中，担心重播会消失。就像昨晚，我正在看电视，到处都找不到重播节目，我感到很恐慌。《教父》正在播出，我换来换去，一个重播都找不到。我当时想，这怎么可能？不过还是有一个重播。那是《保姆》的重播。我和它没有任何共鸣，所以我被卡住了。

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:08.040
<v Ira Glass>Because she's so scared of that happening, Starlee is perpetually cultivating new reruns, forcing yourself to immerse in them. Her latest is Caroline in the City .
<v Ira Glass>因为她太害怕那种情况发生，斯塔莉一直在不断培养新的重播节目，强迫自己沉浸其中。她最近看的是《卡罗琳在城市》。

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:23.780
<v Starlee Kine>When I watch Caroline in the City , it's like I'm really trying to find something, even though I hate it so much, so much. I hate it, every part of it. Hate the way she draws. I hate the way she talks. I hate her assistant, everything.
<v Starlee Kine>当我看《卡罗琳在城市》时，就像我真的在努力寻找什么，尽管我非常非常讨厌它。我讨厌它，它的每一个部分。讨厌她画画的方式。讨厌她说话的方式。讨厌她的助手，一切都讨厌。

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:31.300
<v Ira Glass>And as you've watched Caroline in the City over the course of weeks, do you now actually like it?
<v Ira Glass>随着过去几周你一直看《卡罗琳在城市》，你现在真的喜欢它了吗？

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:39.140
<v Starlee Kine>I don't like it. But I know it. I am very familiar with it.
<v Starlee Kine>我不喜欢它。但我了解它。我非常熟悉它。

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:39.810
<v Ira Glass>And that's enough?
<v Ira Glass>那这就够了吗？

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:44.960
<v Starlee Kine>That's enough.
<v Starlee Kine>这就够了。

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:52.720
<v Ira Glass>What percentage of television is about just straight up comfort and what percentage is about what we think of, traditionally, as entertainment?
<v Ira Glass>电视节目中有多大比例纯粹是为了慰藉，有多大比例是我们传统意义上认为的娱乐？

00:03:52.720 --> 00:04:10.310
<v Starlee Kine>For me? Oh God, 80% is about comfort for me. If something good gets in there it's an accident. Or it's because I feel obligated to watch something good, because I know people are going to ask me the next day.
<v Starlee Kine>对我来说？天哪，对我来说80%是为了慰藉。如果中间掺杂了什么好东西，那纯属偶然。或者是因为我觉得有义务看点好东西，因为我知道第二天会有人问我。

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:29.110
<v Ira Glass>Well, today on our radio program, a defense of not going out into the world and looking for new experiences, a defense of dwelling on what you already know, a defense of staying caught in your own personal reruns. Stories of people who have the same thing going on with some story from their own past that Starlee has with Caroline in the City and Boy Meets World .
<v Ira Glass>好吧，今天在我们的广播节目中，我们要为不走向世界、不寻求新体验进行辩护，为沉湎于已知事物进行辩护，为保持在个人重播中进行辩护。我们要讲一些人的故事，他们对自己过去的故事有着和斯塔莉对《卡罗琳在城市》和《男孩遇见世界》一样的执念。

00:04:29.110 --> 00:05:26.340
<v Ira Glass>From WBEZ Chicago, it is This American Life distributed by Public Radio International. I'm Ira Glass. Our program today in three, yes three, acts. Act One-- Action! Action! Action! In that act the story of what happens when a person, who actually has the power to create reruns, gets stuck in a rerun. Act Two-- Marriage As Rerun. In that act, an exploration, possibly, we think, the first ever, of how in every couple, in every marriage, we are stuck hearing the same stories from our partners over and over, and what we're supposed to think of that. Act Three-- Reruns At The Back Of The Bus. In that act, Sarah Vowell explains what happens when we, as a nation, keep telling ourselves the same political fable over and over long past the point where it makes any sense to. Stay with us.
<v Ira Glass>这里是芝加哥WBEZ广播电台，是美国公共广播国际公司发行的《这就是美国生活》。我是艾拉·格拉斯。我们今天的节目分为三幕，没错，三幕。第一幕——动作！动作！动作！在这一幕里，讲述的是当一个真正有能力创作重播内容的人，自己却陷入重播时会发生什么。第二幕——婚姻如重播。在这一幕里，我们可能第一次探索了每一对夫妻、每一段婚姻中，我们是如何被迫一遍又一遍地听伴侣讲同样的故事，以及我们该如何看待这一点。第三幕——车尾的重播。在这一幕里，莎拉·沃威尔解释了当我们作为一个国家，不断地对自己重复同样的政治寓言，直到它毫无意义时会发生什么。请继续收听。

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:49.510
<v Ira Glass>Act One-- Action! Action! Action! Well, Starlee Kine, who you just met, somebody who loves reruns more than anyone who I've ever known, came upon a rerun moment. An entire film caught in a rerun in a way that dumbfounded even her. The film is called The Beaver Trilogy , and she put together this story about it.
<v Ira Glass>第一幕——动作！动作！动作！好吧，斯塔莉·凯恩，你们刚刚见过，她比我认识的任何人都更爱重播节目，她遇到了一个重播时刻。整部电影以一种连她自己都目瞪口呆的方式陷入了重播。这部电影叫《海狸三部曲》，她为此整理了这个故事。

00:05:49.510 --> 00:06:09.650
<v Starlee Kine>10 minutes into watching The Beaver Trilogy I could already feel how much I'd be talking about it. Once it was over, I felt mournful that I'd never be able to see it again for the first time. Everything about it is so surprising and unexpected, the way movies almost never are. And what  I'm going to try to do right now, here on the radio, is to recreate for you what it's like to see it.
<v Starlee Kine>在看了10分钟《海狸三部曲》后，我就已经感觉到我会为此谈论多久了。一旦结束，我感到很难过，因为我再也没法第一次看到它了。关于它的一切都那么令人惊讶和意想不到，电影几乎从来不是这样的。我现在要尝试做的，就是在广播里，为你还原看到它是什么感觉。

00:06:09.650 --> 00:06:14.710
<v Grooving Gary In The Beaver Trilogy>Are you typing it? Oh, wow. When can I see this?
<v Grooving Gary In The Beaver Trilogy>你在打字吗？哦，哇。我什么时候能看到这个？

