<v Starlee Kine>Don't you love this kid? You love him, but you don't know why you love him, right?
<v Starlee Kine>你不喜欢这个孩子吗？你喜欢他，但你不知道为什么喜欢他，对吧？

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:40.580
<v Grooving Gary In The Beaver Trilogy>Well, my day has come. It's shining.
<v Grooving Gary In The Beaver Trilogy>好吧，我的日子终于来了。它在闪耀。

00:07:40.580 --> 00:08:01.880
<v Starlee Kine>When I saw this in the theater, I couldn't get over what a great idea he was. I loved that someone thought up a character his is so excited just to be taking pictures of a news helicopter parked on a strip of highway. It's only later, after the movie was over, that I learned that I wasn't watching a feature film at all. It's a documentary shot in 1979. This kid's real.
<v Starlee Kine>当我在电影院看到这个时，我对他的伟大创意赞叹不已。我喜欢有人想出一个角色，仅仅因为拍了一架停在公路旁的直升机就如此兴奋。直到电影结束后，我才知道我看的根本不是故事片。这是一部1979年拍摄的纪录片。这孩子是真实的。

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:12.460
<v Trent Harris>Basically, what happened is I was working at a television station in Salt Lake City, and they had a new gadget called a video camera. And I walked out into the parking lot to test out a camera.
