<v Starlee Kine>事实证明，他那天早上刚从比弗开车过来。他的计划是去新闻台，试着上电视。所以当特伦特走近时，简直就像那个比弗男孩一直在等着这一刻。

00:09:09.710 --> 00:09:18.040
<v Grooving Gary In The Beaver Trilogy>But I love hamming it up. You can tell. Well, I'm on TV. I can't believe it. Just in the right place at the right time I guess.
<v Grooving Gary In The Beaver Trilogy>但我喜欢表演。你看得出来。嗯，我上电视了。我简直不敢相信。我想我只是在正确的时间出现在了正确的地点。

00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:37.510
<v Starlee Kine>Part of what makes watching the movie so great is the obvious joy the two of them feel over having found each other. If Trent had wandered out five minutes later, the kid probably would have been heading back home. If the kid had come the next day, Trent wouldn't have been there filming. It was just a lucky accident that they met, and it changed their lives forever.
<v Starlee Kine>让这部电影如此伟大的部分原因，是他们两人在找到彼此后感受到的那种明显的快乐。如果特伦特晚走出来五分钟，那孩子可能已经回家了。如果那孩子第二天来，特伦特就不会在那里拍他。他们相遇纯属幸运的巧合，但这彻底改变了他们的一生。

00:09:37.510 --> 00:09:49.920
<v Trent Harris In The Beaver Trilogy>Dear Trent, how's things going up there? I hope OK. I hope I haven't bothered you in any way with the calls that I have made. If I have, I'm sorry, really.
<v Trent Harris In The Beaver Trilogy>亲爱的特伦特，你在上面过得怎么样？希望一切都好。希望我打来的电话没有打扰到你。如果有的话，我很抱歉，真的。

00:09:49.920 --> 00:10:04.280
<v Starlee Kine>This is the very next scene. There's an image of somebody holding a handwritten note. You have no idea what's happening. And slowly you realize that it's a letter from the Beaver Kid. He's assembled a talent show, and he wants  Trent to come down and film it.
<v Starlee Kine>这是紧接着的一幕。画面中有人拿着一张手写的字条。你根本不知道发生了什么。慢慢地你意识到这是来自比弗男孩的一封信。他组织了一场才艺秀，他想让特伦特去拍下来。

00:10:04.280 --> 00:10:21.200
<v Trent Harris In The Beaver Trilogy>The show is scheduled to come off on the 31st. Please, Trent, come down. I'm begging, I'm pleading. PS, I will be putting on my makeup at the open mortuary at 8:00 AM. You may want to get some shots.
<v Trent Harris In The Beaver Trilogy>表演定在31号。求求你，特伦特，一定要来。我在乞求你，在哀求你。附注：我会在早上8点在露天停尸房化妆。你可能想拍一些镜头。

00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:25.280
<v Grooving Gary In The Beaver Trilogy>Jeez, let's see. How are we going  to do this now?
<v Grooving Gary In The Beaver Trilogy>天哪，让我们看看。现在我们该怎么做呢？

00:10:25.280 --> 00:10:45.510
<v Starlee Kine>And sure enough, the next shot we're at a mortuary, as if that makes any sense at all. The Beaver Kid sits with his hair clipped back away from his face. The local mortician applies eye shadow, mascara, rouge, and lipstick. I'm guessing, because she's the most qualified person in town to do it, but no one explains. The Kid seems different than he was in the parking lot, way more nervous.
<v Starlee Kine>果然，下一个镜头我们就在停尸房了，就好像这有什么逻辑可言似的。比弗男孩坐在那里，头发夹在脑后。当地的殡仪员给他涂上眼影、睫毛膏、胭脂和口红。我猜是因为她是镇上最有资格做这件事的人，但没人解释。那孩子看起来和在停车场时不一样，紧张多了。

00:10:45.510 --> 00:10:51.900
<v Grooving Gary In The Beaver Trilogy>Well, Trent, I think I'll go get into my threads.
<v Grooving Gary In The Beaver Trilogy>好了，特伦特，我想我要去穿我的行头了。

00:10:51.900 --> 00:10:55.530
<v Starlee Kine>The  mortician smiles encouragingly. Let's get you wiggy on, she says.
<v Starlee Kine>殡仪员鼓励地笑了笑。我们给你戴上假发吧，她说。

00:10:55.530 --> 00:10:57.420
<v Mortician In The Beaver Trilogy>Let's get your wiggy on.
<v Mortician In The Beaver Trilogy>让我们给你戴上假发。

00:10:57.420 --> 00:10:58.680
<v Grooving Gary In The Beaver Trilogy>Get my wig on.
<v Grooving Gary In The Beaver Trilogy>戴上我的假发。

00:10:58.680 --> 00:11:07.580
<v Starlee Kine>And pretty soon he's in character, wearing a bulky leather jacket, tight black jeans, and a blond wig that hangs down to his waist. He's supposed to be Olivia Newton-John.
<v Starlee Kine>很快他就进入了角色，穿着厚重的皮夹克，紧身黑牛仔裤，还有一顶垂到腰间的金色假发。他要扮演奥利维亚·纽顿-约翰。

00:11:07.580 --> 00:11:20.500
<v Grooving Gary In The Beaver Trilogy>My purse, Olivia. Well, I really don't know what to say now. I guess I ought to get down in a minute. And I'm off.
<v Grooving Gary In The Beaver Trilogy>我的包，奥利维亚。嗯，我现在真的不知道该说什么了。我想我该下去了。我走了。

00:11:20.500 --> 00:11:36.980
<v Starlee Kine>Watching all this, the thought doesn't occur to you  that the kid's gay or closeted. And I don't think he in fact is. He's more like an overgrown boy dressing up for Halloween, doing the most outrageous thing he can think of. He can barely suppress the giggles as he zips into his knee-high boots. Again, here's Trent.
<v Starlee Kine>看着这一切，你根本不会想到这孩子是同性恋或隐瞒了身份。而且我认为他其实也不是。他更像是个在万圣节打扮自己的长不大的男孩，做着他能想到的最荒谬的事情。当他拉上齐膝靴的拉链时，他几乎抑制不住自己的咯咯笑声。再次重申，这是特伦特。

00:11:36.980 --> 00:11:59.240
<v Trent Harris>You know, I grew up in a small town too, and I know what it's like to be on the outside. It's very difficult. There's an awful lot of pressure from the school, from the church, from your family, from everything to make you conform. And you just can't go around dressing up like Olivia Newton-John without people getting cranky.
<v Trent Harris>你知道，我也是在一个小镇长大的，我知道被排挤是什么感觉。这非常困难。学校、教堂、家人、一切事物都给你巨大的压力，逼你顺从。你可不能随随便便穿得像奥利维亚·纽顿-约翰一样而不让别人抓狂。

00:11:59.240 --> 00:12:10.340
<v Vice Principal In The Beaver Trilogy>For a decade Joan and  Julie [? Kesser ?] have been singing before audiences throughout Beaver County and the state. They have performed on the Eugene Jelesnik Show.
<v Vice Principal In The Beaver Trilogy>十年来，琼和朱莉（凯瑟）一直在比弗县和全州各地的观众面前演唱。她们在尤金·杰莱斯尼克秀上表演过。

00:12:10.340 --> 00:12:18.990
<v Starlee Kine>The next thing you see is a man with a mustache standing on the stage of a school auditorium. He's the Beaver High School vice principal, who the kid has recruited to serve as the talent show MC.
<v Starlee Kine>接下来你看到的是一个留着胡子的男人站在学校礼堂的舞台上。他是比弗高中的副校长，这孩子招募他来担任才艺秀的主持人。

00:12:18.990 --> 00:12:28.380
<v Vice Principal In The Beaver Trilogy>Joan and Julie [? Kesser ?] will now sing "The Happiest Girl in the Whole USA."
<v Vice Principal In The Beaver Trilogy>琼和朱莉（凯瑟）现在将演唱《全美最幸福的女孩》。

00:12:28.380 --> 00:12:37.010
