<v Grooving Gary In The Beaver Trilogy>[MUSIC PLAYING] [SINGING]
<v Grooving Gary In The Beaver Trilogy>（音乐响起）（唱歌）

00:13:24.780 --> 00:13:38.770
<v Starlee Kine>It doesn't matter that he can't really sing, or that he looks nothing like Olivia Newton-John. Watching the kid perform is totally riveting. His eyes are closed, and his face looks pained. He's singing directly into the camera.
<v Starlee Kine>他是不是真的会唱歌，或者他看起来一点也不像奥利维亚·纽顿-约翰，这都无关紧要。看着这孩子表演完全扣人心弦。他闭着眼睛，脸上带着痛苦的表情。他正对着镜头唱歌。

00:13:38.770 --> 00:13:53.210
<v Grooving Gary In The Beaver Trilogy>[SINGING]
<v Grooving Gary In The Beaver Trilogy>（唱歌）

00:13:53.210 --> 00:14:22.300
<v Starlee Kine>It goes on for a long time. It's so long and so raw that you worry. You feel like maybe you shouldn't be watching. It feels too personal. You have no idea what's going to happen next. And at the same time, you're aware he's orchestrated this whole elaborate event at 11:00 on a Saturday morning to a half-empty theater just so he can be up on stage at this moment and be put on TV. It's like watching someone finally get what they've always needed.
<v Starlee Kine>这持续了很长时间。它太长、太原始了，以至于你感到担忧。你会觉得也许你不应该看。这感觉太私人了。你根本不知道接下来会发生什么。与此同时，你意识到他在周六早上11点组织了这场精心策划的活动，在一个半空的剧院里，只是为了让自己能在这一刻登上舞台，出现在电视上。就像看着某人终于得到了他们一直需要的东西。

00:14:22.300 --> 00:14:36.570
<v Starlee Kine>Soon enough, the screen fades to black. Then something happens I never would have seen coming. A new scene opens. A handheld camera shakily approaches a kid taking pictures in the middle of an empty parking lot.
<v Starlee Kine>很快，屏幕淡入黑色。然后发生了一件我从未预料到的事情。新的一幕开始了。手持摄像机晃晃悠悠地接近一个在空旷停车场中间拍照的孩子。

00:14:36.570 --> 00:14:38.770
<v Sean Penn In The Beaver Trilogy>Wow. Are you filming this?
<v Sean Penn In The Beaver Trilogy>哇。你在拍这个吗？

00:14:38.770 --> 00:14:40.920
<v Trent Harris In The Beaver Trilogy>Yeah.
<v Trent Harris In The Beaver Trilogy>是啊。

00:14:40.920 --> 00:14:46.620
<v Sean Penn In The Beaver Trilogy>I can't believe it. I can't believe it. I never been on a set before.
<v Sean Penn In The Beaver Trilogy>我简直不敢相信。我简直不敢相信。我以前从来没上过摄影棚。

00:14:46.620 --> 00:14:55.560
<v Starlee Kine>Everything's exactly the same. Except this time, instead of the Beaver Kid, it's Sean Penn. Sean Penn.
<v Starlee Kine>一切都完全一样。只是这一次，不是比弗男孩，而是肖恩·潘。肖恩·潘。

00:14:55.560 --> 00:14:59.370
<v Sean Penn In The Beaver Trilogy>I'm lucky I came on. I'm an impersonator. I'll do a John Wayne.
<v Sean Penn In The Beaver Trilogy>我很幸运我来了。我是个模仿者。我会来一段约翰·韦恩。

00:14:59.370 --> 00:15:01.650
<v Trent Harris In The Beaver Trilogy>All right, go ahead.
<v Trent Harris In The Beaver Trilogy>好吧，请继续。

00:15:01.650 --> 00:15:15.180
<v Sean Penn In The Beaver Trilogy>Well, I'll tell you out there in TV land, I just made extra, and I'm just tickled to death. I love hamming it up, you can tell.
<v Sean Penn In The Beaver Trilogy>嗯，我会告诉电视机前的各位，我刚拍了加演片段，我真是高兴死了。我喜欢表演，你看得出来。

00:15:15.180 --> 00:15:40.450
<v Starlee Kine>When you watch the movie, there is no explanation for any of this. You have no idea why it's happening again, this time to one of the most famous actors in the world. But I can explain. Shortly after Trent shot the talent show, he moved out to Hollywood with dreams of making it big. But his first film was an unlikely vehicle to stardom. A virtually plotless single character dramatization of the documentary he'd already made. He wrote out a script and started looking for a leading man.
<v Starlee Kine>当你观看这部电影时，对此没有任何解释。你根本不知道为什么这事会再次发生，而且这次是发生在世界上最著名的演员之一身上。但我可以解释。特伦特拍完才艺秀后不久，就怀揣着成名梦搬到了好莱坞。但他的第一部电影并不是通往星途的有利载体。这是一部几乎没有情节、由单一角色演绎他已经拍过的纪录片的电影。他写好了剧本，开始寻找男主角。

00:15:40.450 --> 00:15:54.830
<v Starlee Kine>It was 1981. Sean Penn had just finished filming Fast Times at Ridgemont High , and within a year he'd be a full-fledged movie star. But when Trent found him, Sean Penn was just another unknown actor looking for work. Once again, Trent lucked out.
<v Starlee Kine>那是1981年。肖恩·潘刚拍完《开放的美国学府》，一年内他就会成为真正的电影明星。但特伦特找到他时，肖恩·潘只是另一个等待机会的无名演员。特伦特再次走运了。

00:15:54.830 --> 00:16:04.920
<v Trent Harris>Basically, I didn't have any money. I'm shooting this thing with a home video camera. You can't believe some of the people I auditioned for this, Nick Cage, Eric Stoltz, Anthony Edwards.
<v Trent Harris>基本上，我当时没钱。我用家庭摄像机拍这个。你简直无法相信我为这个角色试镜的人，尼古拉斯·凯奇、埃里克·斯托尔兹、安东尼·爱德华兹。

00:16:04.920 --> 00:16:05.620
<v Starlee Kine>Really?
<v Starlee Kine>真的吗？

00:16:05.620 --> 00:16:59.680
<v Trent Harris>These people all wanted to play this part. And somebody said, you ought to call this guy, Sean Penn, on the phone. I didn't know who he was. I made him an addition for the role. And he came down to the place I was at, and rather than have him read lines, he decided that what he wanted to do was just become the character. And that he would follow me around for for the rest of the day. So he became my cousin Larry from Idaho. And then he just followed me around that day. And I introduced him to people as my cousin from Idaho named Larry. And he acted the part out. And it was really kind of funny, because a year later people would come up to me and say, boy your cousin's really become a big star.
<v Trent Harris>这些人全都想演这个角色。有人说，你应该给这个叫肖恩·潘的家伙打个电话。我不知道他是谁。我让他为这个角色试镜。他来到我所在的地方，他没有读台词，而是决定他想做的就是直接成为这个角色。他会在剩下的时间里跟着我。所以他成了我来自爱达荷州的表弟拉里。然后他那天就一直跟着我。我把他介绍给大家说是我来自爱达荷州的表弟拉里。他演得很入戏。这真的挺有趣的，因为一年后人们还会走到我面前说，天哪，你的表弟真的成了大明星了。

00:16:59.680 --> 00:17:01.790
<v Mortician In The Beaver Trilogy>Let's get your wiggy on.
<v Mortician In The Beaver Trilogy>让我们给你戴上假发。

00:17:01.790 --> 00:17:16.910
<v Sean Penn In The Beaver Trilogy>Let's get my wiggy on, and Olivia will just about be here. Hello, I really don't know quite what to say. I guess we ought to be going.
<v Sean Penn In The Beaver Trilogy>让我们戴上我的假发，奥利维亚很快就到了。你好，我真的不知道该说什么。我想我们该走了。

00:17:16.910 --> 00:17:19.050
<v Starlee Kine>It's practically a shot for shot remake.
<v Starlee Kine>这几乎是一场镜头对镜头的重拍。

00:17:19.050 --> 00:17:46.600
<v Sean Penn In The Beaver Trilogy>[MUSIC PLAYING] [SINGING]
<v Sean Penn In The Beaver Trilogy>（音乐响起）（唱歌）

00:17:46.600 --> 00:18:16.100
<v Starlee Kine>The only difference between this version and the one with the real kid is the ending. After the concert, Sean Penn, whose character's name is Larry, goes home and calls up the director on the phone and asks him not to play the footage on TV. He's worried people will take it the wrong way. The director refuses. Sean Penn drops the phone and picks up a shotgun. He puts the barrel in his mouth and cocks the trigger. [PHONE RINGING] Then the phone rings.
<v Starlee Kine>这一版本和真人版唯一的区别在于结局。演出结束后，肖恩·潘（他的角色名叫拉里）回家给导演打了个电话，请求他不要在电视上播出这段录像。他担心人们会误解。导演拒绝了。肖恩·潘放下电话，拿起一把猎枪。他把枪管放进嘴里，扣动了扳机。（电话铃响）接着电话响了。

00:18:16.100 --> 00:18:17.010
<v Sean Penn In The Beaver Trilogy>Yes.
<v Sean Penn In The Beaver Trilogy>喂。

00:18:17.010 --> 00:18:32.920
<v Carissa In The Beaver Trilogy>Hello, Larry? This is Carissa. Listen, I thought your performance at the talent show was really funny. I can hardly wait to see it on TV. Anyway, I'm having a party Saturday night. Would you like to come and act like Olivia?
<v Carissa In The Beaver Trilogy>喂，拉里？我是卡丽莎。听着，我觉得你在才艺秀上的表演真的很有趣。我迫不及待地想在电视上看到它。不管怎样，我周六晚上有个派对。你想来扮演奥利维亚吗？

00:18:32.920 --> 00:18:59.020
<v Starlee Kine>Sean Penn puts on his Olivia wig, blinks away his tears, and starts singing into a hair brush. It all feels very melodramatic and pat and unbelievable, like a tacked on Hollywood ending. And then the screen goes black. The movie seems to be over. And then, a handheld camera, a parking lot, a kid taking pictures.
<v Starlee Kine>肖恩·潘戴上他的奥利维亚假发，眨掉眼泪，开始对着发刷唱歌。这一切感觉非常伤感、陈腐且不可信，就像是一个生硬的好莱坞结局。然后屏幕变黑。电影似乎结束了。然后，一个手持摄像机，一个停车场，一个拍照的孩子。

00:18:59.020 --> 00:19:01.600
<v Crispin Glover In The Beaver Trilogy>What, why, are you filming this?
<v Crispin Glover In The Beaver Trilogy>什么，为什么，你在拍这个吗？

